            B.q("ai-m4-27", "ai-postgres", "After switching the app's port from 5432 to 6432 (built-in PgBouncer in transaction mode), queries that repeat often start failing with errors that a prepared statement does not exist. psycopg 3 prepares frequently repeated queries automatically. What fixes it on the server side?", listOf("Set pgbouncer.max_prepared_statements to a value above 0", "Change pool_mode to statement", "Move the server to the Burstable tier", "Raise max_connections"), setOf(0), "In transaction mode, consecutive transactions from one client can run on different server connections, so a statement prepared on one is missing on another. Setting pgbouncer.max_prepared_statements above its default of 0 makes PgBouncer track protocol-level prepared statements, which is what psycopg uses.",
